88FB0-589D-4F0A-966F-DFF05CE159DC","B868BD7F-CC6D-418F-95EA-BD8B43354FA3","BCFFEB80-C915-40FF-985D-5D7C7B99586A","C5F1EC58-8972-45C2-9F1F-D5835EF0652C","C835BE8E-EC55-4C2B-8B52-815C66D0209C","D15B6420-1FC0-4130-9AD2-760FD3F31DCD","D47A1D59-69BD-4DEE-9E6A-FCB28AC581B1","D71F4D50-11F3-4B8E-A961-6704FD21D51B","E4DE90A5-20FE-4A8F-B297-163BA41C19C9","EEE05A8E-51CF-4AF4-9509-EC7C64D14D20","F9BD77AC-C360-47DF-8195-D16A4C65DE30","FCEB8EE2-B8A0-44E8-ABD9-EEED4EDDDAA7"],"areaId":"bf7b9b9f675ea769d447a0504ca044027cf9e46621a129e4a6ebd97fb71353fc","issueDateTime":"2026-11-25T23:30:00Z","expiryDateTime":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","avalancheSummary":{"days":[{"date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","content":"\u003cp\u003eMost slopes are safe to travel on as there is very little snow. In the alpine, steer around hard drifts of snow on steep terrain features and below ridgetops. \u003c/p\u003e"}]},"media":{"Images":[{"id":"4d01a0d9-c444-52ac-a7ae-831258e50d78","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795298249/AvIDfx/anf2w8zy6oubrxdjovpf.webp","width":2500,"height":1548,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eSlopes in the Northern Mountains are still quite dry. As you can see in this photo of Square Top Mountain only a few gullies actually have consistent snow. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"Fore- and mid ground slopes are snow free. The alpine slopes in the distance have a shallow coating of snow.","dateTaken":"2026-11-20T17:53:43Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"8f85f756-3c12-5972-8fd4-03de977ca909","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795465867/AvIDfx/o8c2y5zygfk2dwmx8o4t.webp","width":1600,"height":1200,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eLooking northwards at the east-facing ridgeline that extends from the summit of Uneva Peak. You can see that the snow cover is still quite thin in this area.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"Steep, near treeline ridge with a thin coating of snow.","dateTaken":"2026-11-23T20:47:16.593Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"b235454f-9a4f-5d56-8599-00df7e41ffbc","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795298371/AvIDfx/ek4h9jtpddcqiln1dsvn.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eSurfaces in the Northern Mountains are generally very weak but there is no slab to cause an avalanche problem currently. This depth hoar was found near Guanella Pass. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"Large feather like surface hoar.","dateTaken":"2026-11-20T16:29:16Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"e5ed8e17-a921-5d03-b26d-c7c89bdc8a0e","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1794861489/AvIDfx/ksh7ritug6tb8wxzfmg3.webp","width":2500,"height":1406,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThis footage from Coffee Pot road in the Flat Tops shows that although they may look snowy from a distance the coverage is pretty patchy \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A cliff-topped ridge with snowy slopes in the background transitions to forests and then ranches.","dateTaken":"2026-11-14T20:57:53.699Z","isArchived":false}]},"dangerRatings":{"days":[{"position":1,"alp":"low","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z"},{"position":2,"alp":"low","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-27T23:30:00Z"}]},"avalancheProblems":{"days":[[],[]]}},{"id":"74765e1e-0ce6-4921-80fe-7d661fbef3ea","type":"avalancheforecast","polygons":["028E2912-5D1A-4EC6-A22D-2180A797ECDD","071639C0-9D38-49C1-8AF3-F227A80F447D","1660315E-6000-4E83-BF42-36B71129C6B1","3194EF47-46C9-4132-83C1-D156F9B94123","3302D495-0B02-4C2B-B7E2-04A5BC6B732E","35FB8EF6-E22C-48A4-89FA-6FCD49920345","383548A5-2C8E-4CC6-985E-83F7AE17EAB6","4696EB06-4EE3-42DD-B53A-29C3735AD595","54577AA3-268F-4B10-8977-AB30C4206728","6AFB830C-8B2B-4293-AA7A-C872944C2263","6C566741-E85D-427F-8D65-9DC8B58DBCE5","7BA4F5A7-6E11-4A81-88FC-0A72429699A0","97694259-0F92-4CE6-A4C9-3A69D2C33F35","977E9661-AE8E-45A5-9882-EC28C4B149AE","9DFB3103-D688-4AB3-B16D-EE6A20EA25A7","A50331E1-4A1D-4120-8D49-BDBD4BF7914C","B53342B7-BE91-47AD-81A7-21E7074B3FF3","C6D989AD-82E5-4DB9-96A4-15F364D6F09B","D5746397-17D6-4EE2-837F-6DA0AC4CD2D6","D892417F-5570-4940-A311-AA918B8A2AF7","DAFC9825-B67E-4FF5-8E6C-4D05CC20E554","E72F7052-876D-476F-89A0-9AEE369F0317","ED5C21DE-D335-4D82-85CF-485CD449C602"],"areaId":"e3e490f226dce87eaa0715be2e2e76b39eab6e9ac662f1e7166a608419f746f3","issueDateTime":"2026-11-25T23:30:00Z","expiryDateTime":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","avalancheSummary":{"days":[{"date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","content":"\u003cp\u003eYou can still trigger a dangerous avalanche where you encounter older wind-drifted slabs below ridgelines, especially on northwest through north to east-facing slopes at upper elevations. You might trigger them from thin spots above, adjacent to, or below the drifted features. Choose wind-sheltered terrain to avoid the problem.\u003c/p\u003e"}]},"media":{"Images":[{"id":"8e7c0fc4-009e-59c0-8afe-cc96c05fd2e9","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795552311/AvIDfx/bjzzbdlvi8exfntemg4x.webp","width":1080,"height":1440,"credit":"CAIC","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThis recent avalanche near Independence Pass is a great example of the type of terrain where you can trigger an avalanche. Cross-loaded gullies like this have a stiff slab sitting on weak snow below that takes time to break down. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A fresh avalanche with a ski track next to it.","dateTaken":"2026-11-23T20:31:54.646Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"47c25326-9f80-50df-91ad-68cd8ae1e457","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795302869/AvIDfx/r3jdmmb2l54bcezzgvvz.webp","width":330,"height":330,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eRemotely triggered avalanches near Independence Pass from Saturday November 21\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"Looking at an avalanche.","dateTaken":"2026-11-21T23:17:13.322Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"b49acaa0-c9d1-52e4-a779-c95c59bd7093","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795552477/AvIDfx/pkrbjfbomtghdwvywx7f.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"Public","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThis large natural avalanche highlights the most dangerous terrain right now. Steep NW-N-E-facing slopes where stiffer slabs have formed are prime places to trigger an avalanche. The larger the slope, the higher the chances of getting buried. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A large avalanche below a rocky ridgeline","dateTaken":"2026-11-22T18:24:20Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"ff73ba03-b500-5c45-8075-7b43f4b4a441","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795295511/AvIDfx/vmovcfihu9koxst0ekez.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"Dylan Craaybeek","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThis avalanche was triggered from around 300 feet away on a northeast-facing slope near treeline in Yule Creek, between Marble and Crested Butte.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"Looking across a snowy slope at an avalanche.","dateTaken":"2026-11-21T17:37:48Z","isArchived":false}]},"dangerRatings":{"days":[{"position":1,"alp":"moderate","tln":"moderate","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z"},{"position":2,"alp":"moderate","tln":"moderate","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-27T23:30:00Z"}]},"avalancheProblems":{"days":[[{"type":"persistentSlab","aspectElevations":["nw_alp","n_alp","ne_alp","e_alp","nw_tln","n_tln","ne_tln","e_tln"],"likelihood":"possible","expectedSize":{"min":"1.0","max":"2.0"}}],[{"type":"persistentSlab","aspectElevations":["nw_alp","n_alp","ne_alp","e_alp","nw_tln","n_tln","ne_tln","e_tln"],"likelihood":"possible","expectedSize":{"min":"1.0","max":"2.0"}}]]}},{"id":"e26aac4d-e440-4df2-9941-e2350e91841f","type":"avalancheforecast","polygons":["468B78D0-198E-4FA4-A2CD-09F436CBA5EE","4FB2A5B0-EE82-4734-86BD-AECECDA73A07","72283DBC-55B0-4638-A44E-7420893000C5","7696EB7F-C450-4967-B4BF-C4928C6F82D0","7E3F4D07-B8FB-49CB-8B24-F67304294AEA","FE996429-CEFA-41FC-8228-3E4661406DDF"],"areaId":"b99916e5c4f11223d2e1cd44a246ec62c91fa23f8717bffe13344c819abbffd3","issueDateTime":"2026-11-25T23:30:00Z","expiryDateTime":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","avalancheSummary":{"days":[{"date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","content":"\u003cp\u003eMost slopes are safe to travel. The snowpack is generally too thin and soft for a dangerous avalanche. A rare wind-drifted feature above a steep planar slope would be the one type of feature to steer around.\u003c/p\u003e"}]},"media":{"Images":[{"id":"6cfe94e9-c828-515e-b45b-2fbdf8a205b6","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795554360/AvIDfx/xeai1zmiyk80li23vzvp.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"CAIC","caption":"\u003cp\u003eIn a few deeper places on shady slopes where stiffer slabs sit on weak snow below, you could trigger a small avalanche. These are isolated to planar, wind-drifted slopes, so keep an eye out. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A snow pit showing a stability test with ruler","dateTaken":"2026-11-23T20:46:12Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"df6a902d-33dd-519e-9999-11182873e57c","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795296817/AvIDfx/zrbqdowfaexw41sbh2u9.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eWhile this observation is not from Grand Mesa, it shows the kind of small avalanche on a wind drifted feature you may be able to trigger. Triggering an avalanche like this is unlikely and generally inconsequential unless triggered above a steep cliff. South San Juan Mountains.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A small avalanche with small trees nearby, blue skies, and a feature that looks impacted by wind.","dateTaken":"2026-11-18T21:33:43.718Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"68bdfc6f-d9a2-51cd-b6f5-87a8407a2b28","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795382175/AvIDfx/jaw4araqbtyxactsslzi.webp","width":2500,"height":3333,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eSteep creek banks with shallow weak snow may be another place you could find an avalanche. This photo is from a different zone, but is a good illustration of the kind of avalanche you may find along a creek bank. With the current shallow snow coverage many creeks carry open water and or weak snow bridges making these terrain traps more dangerous.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A small avalanche on a steep creek bank slope with debris in the gully below","dateTaken":"2026-11-21T21:22:36.926Z","isArchived":false}]},"dangerRatings":{"days":[{"position":1,"alp":"noRating","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z"},{"position":2,"alp":"noRating","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-27T23:30:00Z"}]},"avalancheProblems":{"days":[[],[]]}},{"id":"2cae4022-3650-4a5f-9f88-873add900ae8","type":"avalancheforecast","polygons":["0BFCE84E-A2A4-4986-BF7D-84C1A0A2E467","0EF68DA6-9B2C-4366-BF30-4256AE6340BA","20D852D8-E47A-4447-ABE2-05E5F5E022D0","21F30165-D180-48B5-A36F-830F4DA1E8ED","30232C29-4A0C-4D7A-B951-EF7B873C2CBF","46C849AB-16F5-441C-9320-D501C858D14A","59C37E11-7808-47BD-9C61-8D4F6F7F2A04","72121255-B904-4013-887A-6A179A9C128B","7CC67C5D-EB4A-4F64-B82C-280ECE3C7F3C","85EBF9CD-C3F3-440B-8078-35A764C4FB9A","8DE3AC50-C0E1-417D-9F44-70F6A8F75F31","90E4159E-4E27-45EA-BA30-7A3D1894BE39","9F9C1CD8-E0D0-41B0-BD76-6BCC5DA8033E","A2D10799-F26B-475F-A19D-558A8B316594","A673FFED-CD79-4281-8CF4-AA2432ACFA2B","AC2CF19C-8218-433B-BF5A-994FCEA118FE","C37659DF-724F-4A19-B0F3-C3B490F20E56","D77686B4-1A5C-4D39-8EE8-7F8A53FCC702","DD137A25-003B-48F7-903C-0F8ECC273F8E","DE3D5E00-3003-4912-8C5C-7E6E1D752490","EE15BE29-A2EF-4CAD-A0A4-C05CC09E4549","EFE54733-51A7-48EE-B871-EE798C6197AA"],"areaId":"894e51d2c85fc4bf770c35add465d964d9545724dff415a9514abfeb6d48a670","issueDateTime":"2026-11-25T23:30:00Z","expiryDateTime":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","avalancheSummary":{"days":[]},"media":{"Images":[]},"dangerRatings":{"days":[{"position":1,"alp":"noForecast","tln":"noForecast","btl":"noForecast","date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z"},{"position":2,"alp":"noForecast","tln":"noForecast","btl":"noForecast","date":"2026-11-27T23:30:00Z"}]},"avalancheProblems":{"days":[[],[]]}},{"id":"251fb79e-a558-41df-bf92-e769b5cebcfb","type":"avalancheforecast","polygons":["0E5A5DFF-7518-494A-AD5E-7C20A1F98FFD","242191AB-2749-4585-A09B-C274A1C196D8","288624C3-E0C0-4816-86A1-57B068E20D5F","428340C8-91A8-480A-8FB8-322EAB7CD9EB","4765FB8A-C436-45FA-9684-6E79CF4C6ECD","568FD9F5-9079-4965-BD83-8DD1577C9141","674FEC54-6A25-4F1B-9201-B145C6C609E0","6BE87E45-0574-4512-907F-EC3B9EBCA365","8908D9DD-0DED-4577-A8B4-6D8E48407182","93EA98DD-4165-4B8D-97F7-FE0774706466","98E60E8A-5124-454F-9660-9B879AE63B09","A3B7D9A2-121A-41EA-B824-ADCB4B1323A3","B4DBB658-8373-4DAB-8D42-7ABA0564AF9E","CB25CEAA-D3C0-416C-B11B-60B3BFF39F34","D6E3810F-1A94-4173-A5AD-147EEC39E464","D7362528-9E1C-4B04-ACEA-70E4F9BFB8B7","DBC40A27-66D6-4C9D-927E-1D5F05092F1A","E687FCD9-066C-4E47-8B6C-164C1B586A18","ECA6DAA1-1E5C-4D1F-8186-B9969A5E9EAD","EEF9E8C9-3899-4E76-8A11-C2265812FA53","F2A935D9-8E28-4421-8382-837E3E0E99B7","FCDD2204-2B10-4061-8CDF-928C5DE4C24D","FD36A9C3-DDBD-43BF-BA4B-AE2D2C8CA87F"],"areaId":"94a3aa9cbc76396910c46bb5c1bc7779ad7f065827aeed290a4ea39ac568e1e2","issueDateTime":"2026-11-25T23:30:00Z","expiryDateTime":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","avalancheSummary":{"days":[{"date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","content":"\u003cp\u003eYou can trigger a slab avalanche near and above treeline on the north half of the compass on slopes steeper than about 30 degrees. These avalanches can be large enough to bury or injury you. Give drifted slopes a wide berth; you might trigger them from above, next to, or below.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eSeek out wind-sheltered areas and slopes below treeline for safer travel options.\u003c/p\u003e"}]},"media":{"Images":[{"id":"701036ff-23de-5dab-9e09-89cb12ee4767","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795641618/AvIDfx/ujnywc02b1z24p7vgq3l.webp","width":480,"height":640,"credit":"Sandy East","caption":"\u003cp\u003eA skier triggered D1.5 Persistent Slab avalanche on a west-facing slope above treeline.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A snowy slope with ski tracks next to a recent avalanche.","dateTaken":"2026-11-24T21:48:16Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"0865b384-b0d7-510f-9571-fefdebb11b4e","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795381834/AvIDfx/w6baqz7nducx5ugyuqid.webp","width":2500,"height":3333,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eIntense winds on Tuesday and Friday this week transported huge amounts of snow and built thick, stiff slabs on leeward convexities like the one picture here. It's hard to tell what is crown versus cornice in this photo, but recent avalanches have broken as deep as 6 feet in this wind-loaded areas. We recorded more D2 avalanches, large enough to kill a human, on Saturday than any day so far this season. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A skier standing next to large avalanche debris. ","dateTaken":"2026-11-21T20:11:26Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"0dd78e27-4ccb-5fb8-a4d3-a83eb14f0333","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795382047/AvIDfx/hqps4dj363u3yykiu89q.webp","width":2500,"height":1092,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eThis avalanche from Saturday was remotely-triggered by riders as they descended an adjacent slope and it perfectly illustrates our Persistent Slab avalanche problem. \u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A snowboarder standing looking back at an avalanche they triggered. ","dateTaken":"2026-11-21T19:51:37Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"8d46cf16-3063-58d3-aa78-8f30ff263a91","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795641344/AvIDfx/uj4ztw96kbpteizkwjic.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"Bruce Erikson","caption":"\u003cp\u003eA large Persistent Slab avalanche on a northeast-facing slope above treeline.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A snowy ridge line with an avalanche and adjacent ski tracks.","dateTaken":"2026-11-22T18:06:48Z","isArchived":false}]},"dangerRatings":{"days":[{"position":1,"alp":"moderate","tln":"moderate","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z"},{"position":2,"alp":"moderate","tln":"moderate","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-27T23:30:00Z"}]},"avalancheProblems":{"days":[[{"type":"persistentSlab","aspectElevations":["w_alp","nw_alp","n_tln","n_alp","ne_alp","ne_tln","e_alp","e_tln","w_tln","nw_tln"],"likelihood":"possible","expectedSize":{"min":"1.0","max":"2.0"}}],[{"type":"persistentSlab","aspectElevations":["w_alp","nw_alp","n_tln","n_alp","ne_alp","ne_tln","e_alp","e_tln","w_tln","nw_tln"],"likelihood":"possible","expectedSize":{"min":"1.0","max":"2.0"}}]]}},{"id":"7ea4e424-02ef-48d5-806b-0c1c471efc06","type":"avalancheforecast","polygons":["143F9D35-8EA3-49C4-812D-D87C0A6DD0F4","1EAF86F5-A2D8-44B7-A485-CF625FC37C72","5E3087F6-0962-463C-B1DC-D702EC792F3B","5F219827-0BDB-4106-924F-2483CCFB5F51","6952335B-D6BA-4FD0-BE76-0D1012DCF708","80965A3A-9069-422B-BD91-E0EABDFD44FE","8F48A7FC-A784-473E-BD34-0F789B505D14","A03BDED3-E2F8-4E90-815E-397C421D386E","A1C44D1C-F76B-4597-832C-BA12E47501AF","A2D787FE-207C-489C-83F1-63715DEF6E7A","E431262C-0AE0-4E4B-9DA4-A2E35B49E671","EC9276F5-8C4A-431C-882B-4BA90A9D8881"],"areaId":"e64195fa244e31e2c14e728de1a1e4200c471c3da41d10eca60680c9ed03fcca","issueDateTime":"2026-11-25T23:30:00Z","expiryDateTime":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","avalancheSummary":{"days":[{"date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z","content":"\u003cp\u003eMost slopes are safe from avalanches due to thin and discontinuous snow cover. You can trigger a small avalanche in wind-drifted snow above treeline. Look for these drifts below ridges and around rocky outcrops on slopes facing west through north to east.\u003c/p\u003e"}]},"media":{"Images":[{"id":"5f5ef023-3d09-5890-8218-17304ab45039","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795210883/AvIDfx/gbz7bayxncwpidp0ebei.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eAbove treeline, you could find isolated pockets of stiff, wind-drifted snow. These are the most likely areas to trigger a small avalanche. Wind drifted pockets often feel stiff and look pillowy.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A pole with a crack in the snow. ","dateTaken":"2026-11-17T20:59:36Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"a3f5512c-fc1f-5019-ba6b-7fa3c7498ece","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795211049/AvIDfx/gcgfao5sa5aqtyc6neyn.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eExpect generally safe avalanche conditions across the region because most slopes still don't have enough snow to produce avalanches, like Buckeye Peak, near Fremont Pass.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"A mountain that is mostly dry except for a little bit of snow on top. ","dateTaken":"2026-11-16T19:58:33Z","isArchived":false},{"id":"e09031a4-fb60-5252-8f5e-06152716411a","url":"http://res.cloudinary.com/dozsqvbas/image/upload/v1795211152/AvIDfx/d5nntsj8jdnffpny6siz.webp","width":2500,"height":1875,"credit":"","caption":"\u003cp\u003eRecent strong winds pressed snow in the alpine into thin and pockety slabs, especially below ridgelines and around rocky couloirs. This photo was taken during a strong wind event on Tuesday, November 17th near Twin Lakes. Additional wind and minimal precipitation on the 20th likely pressed snow into additional isolated features.\u003c/p\u003e","tag":"avalanche","altText":"Winds blowing snow over a mountain ridge. ","dateTaken":"2026-11-17T21:47:41.639Z","isArchived":false}]},"dangerRatings":{"days":[{"position":1,"alp":"low","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-26T23:30:00Z"},{"position":2,"alp":"low","tln":"low","btl":"low","date":"2026-11-27T23:30:00Z"}]},"avalancheProblems":{"days":[[],[]]}}]